  "analytic_review_groups": [
    {
      "topic": "Flag setup",
      "review": "Connected compact X, global smooth prime flag and adapted coordinates; residual restrictions use the earlier normal bundles."
    },
    {
      "topic": "One-dimensional leaves",
      "review": "Lexicographic minimum and its nonzero Taylor-coefficient functional give induction on finite-dimensional V; distinct finite values cannot cancel."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Gauduchon degrees",
      "review": "Positive a_i and a_n=1; residual zero divisor contains the next flag member with its valuation multiplicity."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Linear valuation bound",
      "review": "Degree recursion includes all earlier normal-bundle degrees with their signs; absolute values give finite nonnegative recursive C_i."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Additive semigroup",
      "review": "Connectedness makes products of nonzero sections nonzero; S has only its origin at degree zero."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Closed convex body",
      "review": "Linear valuation bounds give a compact height-one cone slice; empty positive-degree algebra is kept separate."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Ambient upper count",
      "review": "Disjoint scaled half-open cubes lie in shrinking compact neighborhoods; continuity of volume proves limsup and the empty-interior consequence."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Semigroup input",
      "review": "The accepted SGPT Theorem C.2.1 input is used with full group generation and compact strongly nonnegative cone; no fresh external recertification is asserted."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Primitive lattice count",
      "review": "One-dimensional leaves identify degree-m semigroup points with dim W_m in the full-lattice case."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Degree splitting",
      "review": "Degree projection equals eZ and horizontal lattice has rank d; g_0 may be chosen in G without requiring it to lie in S."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Affine dimension",
      "review": "Normalized positive-degree semigroup points span span_R G and have height one, giving affine dimension d."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Restricted coordinate map",
      "review": "The cone is intersected with span_R G before the linear coordinate isomorphism; the original horizontal linear bound survives with height q=m/e."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Intrinsic volume scale",
      "review": "The height-one body becomes e(Delta-b/e), and coordinate volume is e^d times translated Lambda-volume."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Period and zero dimension",
      "review": "Only multiples of e can support sections; positivity implies eventual nonvanishing, and d=0 integer dimensions are eventually one."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Section-ratio field",
      "review": "Products give common homogeneous denominators; inversion of a nonzero ratio and W_0=C give a field."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Transcendence lower bound",
      "review": "Common powers of d+1 sections with affinely independent normalized values produce d ratios with independent valuations; finite polynomial minima cannot cancel."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Transcendence upper bound",
      "review": "A common positive-degree denominator produces binomial(q+r,r) independent sections; intrinsic O(q^d) forces r<=d."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Flag independence",
      "review": "Field and supported degrees fix d and e; the identical normalized graded-dimension limit fixes intrinsic volume."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Kahler modification and mass",
      "review": "Smooth reduction uses the prior metric proposition; domination, exceptional-set change of variables, semipositive determinant monotonicity and Stokes give a uniform bound."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Moishezon consequence",
      "review": "Full-dimensional body gives n independent meromorphic functions and the accepted projective-modification input; BMP failure therefore forces zero ambient volume."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Point blowup",
      "review": "Dimension-one identity and higher-dimensional exceptional projective flag are separate; Hartogs extension and the identity theorem preserve section spaces and products."
    },
    {
      "topic": "All compact section counts",
      "review": "Pullback preserves graded dimensions, supported degrees and section-ratio fields, making d,e,V independent of the auxiliary modification."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Non-Moishezon bound",
      "review": "Apply the complete count to the full section ring; d=n forces Moishezon, while empty positive-degree rings stay separate. Weighted spaces receive only inclusion upper bounds; Jacobian corrections are retained."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Hopf body and figure",
      "review": "Successive monomial division leaves a nowhere-zero elliptic residual section; all tuples occur and k>0 simplex lattice volume matches binomial growth. k=0 remains a point. The displayed threefold triangle has area k^2/2 and zero ambient volume."
    }
  ],
